# clang-tidy checks of the kernel-mode driver (driver/kmd and driver/shim): tools/quality/kmd_tidy.py.
# The set is chosen for state defects: values that nobody reads, branches that do the same thing, conditions that
# are always true or always false, and switches that do not handle every state. tools/quality/kmd_tidy_baseline.txt
# records the findings of the day the gate started; a new finding fails the gate (docs/testing/kmd-static-checks.md).
#
# Disabled checks and the reason for each:
#   clang-analyzer-security.*                    - insecureAPI asks for memcpy_s and friends, which the kernel CRT
#                                                  does not have; nothing in it is about state.
#   clang-analyzer-unix.*, clang-analyzer-cplusplus.*, clang-analyzer-osx.*, clang-analyzer-fuchsia.*,
#   clang-analyzer-webkit.*, clang-analyzer-optin.*, clang-analyzer-nullability.*
#                                                - APIs and annotations the driver does not use (POSIX, C++, Apple,
#                                                  Fuchsia, WebKit); optin.* are portability and performance rules.
#   bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters         - names the shape of the WDK DDIs (two ULONGs next to each other);
#                                                  hundreds of findings, none of them a state defect.
#   bugprone-reserved-identifier                 - the WDK naming style (_BC250_DEVICE) is the kit's convention.
#   bugprone-narrowing-conversions               - register arithmetic with ULONG and UCHAR fields everywhere; /W4
#                                                  of the build already sees the conversions that lose bits.
#   bugprone-implicit-widening-of-multiplication-result
#                                                - the same register arithmetic; no finding is about state.
#   bugprone-macro-parentheses                   - style of macros, not behaviour; the imported AMD macros fail it.
#   bugprone-multi-level-implicit-pointer-conversion, bugprone-casting-through-void
#                                                - void** out-parameters are the WDK DDI convention.
#   bugprone-signed-bitwise                      - C promotes every UCHAR and USHORT operand to int, so each shift
#                                                  of a register byte is a finding; the build's /W4 sees real
#                                                  sign problems.
#   bugprone-suspicious-string-compare           - if (memcmp(...)) and if (!wcscmp(...)) are the driver's idiom
#                                                  for "differs" and "equal"; the check wants an explicit != 0.
#   bugprone-suspicious-include                  - the build includes .inc and .c parts on purpose (state_contract.c,
#                                                  hdmi_link_stream.inc and the other split units).
#   bugprone-assignment-in-if-condition is ON on purpose: an assignment in a condition is a write of state that a
#                                                  reader does not see as one.
#
# Compiler warnings that are checks here: clang-diagnostic-switch (a switch over an enum without a case for a
# value and without a default) and clang-diagnostic-switch-enum (a switch over an enum without a case for a value,
# also with a default). kmd_tidy.py adds -Wswitch-enum to the command for the second one.
Checks: >
  -*,
  clang-analyzer-core.*,
  clang-analyzer-deadcode.*,
  clang-analyzer-valist.*,
  bugprone-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-reserved-identifier,
  -bugprone-narrowing-conversions,
  -bugprone-implicit-widening-of-multiplication-result,
  -bugprone-macro-parentheses,
  -bugprone-multi-level-implicit-pointer-conversion,
  -bugprone-casting-through-void,
  -bugprone-signed-bitwise,
  -bugprone-suspicious-string-compare,
  -bugprone-suspicious-include,
  misc-redundant-expression,
  clang-diagnostic-switch,
  clang-diagnostic-switch-enum
WarningsAsErrors: ''
HeaderFilterRegex: '.*[\\/]driver[\\/](kmd|shim)[\\/].*'
